# The Emperor's death and Baurus's farewell. After the Amulet is handed over (74) the final assassin (CGAssassinFinal)
# kills the Emperor (CGEmperorScript sets 76) and the quest sets 80; the assassin attacks the player and Baurus. The
# player kills him (84), Baurus kneels by the Emperor (85, 86) and force-greets the player. The player asks the Baurus
# chain (CGBaurusA..I); "The sewers?" sets 87, which opens the class menu; "What about you?" sets 88, which starts MQ02
# (stages 10 and 20) and adds the Amulet/Blades/Jauffre topics.

case baurus_emperor_dies
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 76
expect UrielSeptimRef.GetDead
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 80
end

# The assassin is hostile to the player from stage 80; kill stands in for the fight (god mode is on).
case baurus_kill_assassin
run
CGAssassinFinal.kill
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 84
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 85
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 86
hear 1800 BaurusRef We've failed
end

# Baurus's force-greet ("We've failed...") opens the dialogue on its own; the topics are the CGBaurus chain, each choice
# leading to the next: A "The Emperor gave it to me." -> B -> C -> D (gives the sewer key) -> E "The sewers?" (stage 87).
case baurus_topics
wait 30
ask "The Emperor gave it to me."
ask "I must take it to Jauffre."
ask "There is another heir."
ask "How do I get there?"
expect player.GetItemCount CGExitKey >= 1
ask "The sewers?"
until 300 GetStage Charactergen >= 87
end

# Menu expected: the class menu, asked through TES4_Chargen.Ask like the birthsign, so `pick` names the row (CLAS
# FULL). Baurus then re-greets ("I thought so. A few rats and goblins ...").
case baurus_class_menu
pick Warrior
hear 900 BaurusRef I thought so
wait 30
ask "After the sewers, then what?"
ask "Yes, I understand."
ask "What about you? What will you do?"
until 300 GetStage Charactergen >= 88
expect GetStageDone MQ02 10
expect GetStageDone MQ02 20
expect GetQuestRunning MQ02
end
